  "selected": [
    {
      "id": "cmip6-bgc-units-per-volume",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-bgc-units-per-volume.md",
      "sha256": "30d729792e1986dd91c822785512ceabe336ef10a47f0a7db602802e5425d70b",
      "reason": "All CMIP6/OMIP BGC tracers are stored per unit volume (mol m-3) while WOA23 oxygen is per unit mass, so the µmol kg-1 concentrations and the 20/60 thresholds require a density-based conversion of the model fields before comparison.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Model `o2` is mol m-3: convert to µmol kg-1 as µmol kg-1 = mmol m-3 × 1000/ρ using the in-situ density (`compute_potential_density_anomaly`, `ref_pressure=None`), not `transform_unit`'s constant default; state the density used (`attrs['density_assumption']`).",
        "The total O2 inventory in moles is a volume integral of the native mol m-3 field with `convert_concentration_to_content` and `volcello` — no density; passing a converted µmol kg-1 field instead applies the default density and biases the inventory by about 1%."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "common-comparison-mask",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/common-comparison-mask.md",
      "sha256": "bbb98200f52b4a692ce097704b8c438179a795a44bec6b856c03cf31931af4ea",
      "reason": "Bias/volume statistics between models and between a model and WOA23 exist only where all fields have data, so one mask must be built over the model fields and WOA23 and applied to every field, and WOA23's own land-sea mask must not be imposed on comparisons it is not part of.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Comparing global OMZ volumes is a difference of means each taken over its own domain, not a bias on a shared mask; report each on its own grid and say so. `ocean_only=True` is right because WOA23 is the reference.",
        "Build any mask per depth level (coverage shrinks with depth) and report the cell counts alongside the metrics."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "anomaly-baselines-and-climate-indices",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/anomaly-baselines-and-climate-indices.md",
      "sha256": "e0afb5c187aca1e075f9549153b1e896320bb0539544f66d3293fab4b4b77c92",
      "reason": "The reference is a 1971-2000 climate normal and the scenario window is 2071-2100, so the baseline each field is expressed against (and the offset it introduces) must be stated rather than treating the two periods as directly interchangeable.",
      "status": "not_applicable",
      "not_applicable_reason": "no anomaly removal, climate index, baseline choice or seasonal aggregation is requested; the scenario change is a difference of two 30-year period means."
    },
    {
      "id": "monthly-means-are-time-averages",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "pitfalls/monthly-means-are-time-averages.md",
      "sha256": "df6b5c23460f88f1522e5c6a665e1efbb8322c3ae876c885530f3019aa284ee0",
      "reason": "The OMZ volume/thickness below a threshold is a nonlinear diagnostic of monthly-mean o2, so thresholds applied offline to monthly means differ from the mean of the instantaneous diagnostic and from the online quantity.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "A threshold exceedance is nonlinear: state the order used — diagnostic-then-average (per-month OMZ volume, then period mean) or average-then-diagnostic (OMZ of the period-mean field, the like-for-like choice against the WOA23 climatology).",
        "Average monthly fields over the periods with `temporal_aggregate(freq='mean')` for day weights; `compute_basic_stat(op='mean', dim='time')` weights every calendar month equally and is not a time average."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "historical-ssp245-member-continuity",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "pitfalls/historical-ssp245-member-continuity.md",
      "sha256": "02341c56015c6296db14585b4561fc32ca6b4e52e2264bec50eee6746c1d55f6",
      "reason": "ssp245 continues the historical member named in parent_variant_label, so historical→ssp245 differences can mix forced change with internal variability when the local historical member differs, and this qualifies the percentage-change numbers.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "GFDL-ESM4 and MPI-ESM1-2-LR historical r1i1p1f1 followed by ssp245 r1i1p1f1 is one continuous trajectory, so their period difference is valid; CESM2 ssp245 is r10i1p1f1 and historical r10i1p1f1 is absent, so no change can be formed for CESM2 — label it as such."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-o2sat-and-derived-oxygen",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-o2sat-and-derived-oxygen.md",
      "sha256": "afe46747641c91aff8ddc9f50165a800a7c64d5d2e39b50e816280d02e59fba3",
      "reason": "WOA23 AOU and percent saturation use the observational solubility formula and mass units while o2sat/AOU for the models are per volume, so the WOA23 AOU and saturation values inside the 60-threshold OMZ must be interpreted on their own definitions.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Convert model `o2` to µmol kg-1 before thresholding: `identify_oxygen_minimum_zone` compares the field with the threshold in the field's own units (the 20 and 60 µmol kg-1 levels).",
        "WOA23 AOU and percent saturation rest on WOA's own solubility and pressure conventions; state that differences from the model's OMIP recipe are partly definitional."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-static-grid-fields",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-static-grid-fields.md",
      "sha256": "2ad0548ca0993fa57d8f1fad27a267dcf9c0e1d007a74343d4bbdbf5b4f1ca17",
      "reason": "volcello and areacello define tracer-cell volume and area (layer thickness = volcello/areacello), which is exactly what is needed to convert an oxygen threshold to a water volume and to sum layer thicknesses into a column OMZ thickness.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "OMZ volume = Σ `volcello` over cells below the threshold; column thickness uses `cell_thickness_like` (volcello/areacello), which respects partial bottom cells — `lev_bnds` differences fail there (GFDL-ESM4: 14% of cells differ by >1%; MPI partial steps up to ±50% in 3.3% of cells).",
        "`deptho` is model bathymetry; total ocean area differs by about a per cent between models, so report the domain each integral covers rather than rescaling."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "basin-and-region-definitions",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/basin-and-region-definitions.md",
      "sha256": "d0d90c32fab9f6e0a39d4f769a4e902e6412b2ad1b09d9c7d19f6bb3aa426611",
      "reason": "The Pacific/Indian/Atlantic volumes depend on which basin partition is used (marginal seas folded in, Southern and Arctic separated), so the basin statistic must state the WOA23 mask's convention.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "The Ofx `basin` field is not in the local archive: take basins from the WOA23 mask via `select_basin`/`load_basin_mask` with `include_marginal_seas=True` (folds marginal seas into the parent ocean) and state the mask used.",
        "State the `depth_dependent` choice: surface labels applied through the column (`False`) is what a named ocean usually means; per-level labels (`True`) are what a water-mass analysis wants."
      ]
    }
